{"t": 1794119134.0097067, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "Pipeline fix for `main` (pipeline #8812, sha `a91c2e0`)\n\n**What was red**\nThe `test:contract` job (job #77104) failed on `main`:\n\n```\ncontract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format\nAssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\n**Root cause**\n`billing/invoice.py` built the invoice number with `f\"INV-{year}-{seq}\"`, so the sequence was not padded. The contract test encodes the Finance ERP import requirement (FIN-77): the sequence part must be zero-padded to 6 digits. For seq 42 the service emitted `INV-2026-42` instead of `INV-2026-000042`, so the contract test failed.\n\n**Fix**\n`billing/invoice.py` now formats the sequence with `:06d`:\n\n```python\nreturn f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\nVerified locally: `invoice_number(2026, 42)` -> `INV-2026-000042`, and wider sequences (e.g. 123456) are unchanged.\n\n**Relevance to this MR**\nThis MR switches invoices to the ERP v2 format. The ERP v2 invoice number must keep the zero-padded 6-digit sequence (`INV-<year>-<seq:06d>`); otherwise the contract test `test_invoice_number_format` will fail again after merge. The fix above is the minimal change that makes `main` green and matches the ERP v2 contract.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
